    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1162">

                <pb facs="1007" n="903" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg903"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.52/77.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Embassy of Spain</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-12-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 12, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My dear Mr. Counselor</hi>: The news which I had the
                    honour to communicate to you this morning, verbally and by note, regarding the
                    menace of Francisco Villa to Spaniards residing in Chihuahua, has been confirmed
                    by a telegram which I have just received from the Spanish Minister in Mexico,
                    who informs me that 400 Spaniards have been ordered to leave the State of
                    Chihuahua in ten days’ time and <pb facs="1008" n="904" xml:id="pg904"/> to
                    abandon their properties, under pain of death, if these orders are not complied
                    with.</p>
                <p>I need not dwell upon the gravity of the situation and I trust that the United
                    States Government will spare no effort to ensure the protection of the lives and
                    properties of my compatriots.</p>
                <p>Believe me [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Juan Riaño</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
